Make the shader disk cache after a state load when the title ID is unchanged

Loading a save state rebuilds the whole emulated system, GPU and renderer
included (System::serialize, input archive: Shutdown then Init). The new
renderer's PipelineCache starts with program ID 0 and NO shader disk cache:
LoadDefaultDiskResources, which makes it, is called by the frontends only when
a game boots. Upstream then calls SwitchDiskResources with the running title's
ID, and SwitchDiskCache is written to make the cache when there is none ("NOTE:
curr_disk_cache can be null if emulation restarted without calling
LoadDefaultDiskResources").

SwitchCache never reaches it when the title ID is 0, the ID of any homebrew
without one: 0 equals the new cache's default, so it returns early ("already
using cache for title_id") with no disk cache, and the next draw dereferences
it (PipelineCache::UseProgrammableVertexShader -> ShaderDiskCache, this=0x0).
Seen in Retro Pal's host harness (Tools/3ds-bench roundtrip) on 2026-10-16:
every state load of such a program crashed. A game with a real title ID
differs from 0 and goes through SwitchDiskCache, which is why commercial games
do not meet it.

The early return now also requires a disk cache to exist, so SwitchCache goes
on to SwitchDiskCache, which makes one. After it, the same harness loads the
state and replays 300 frames: sound identical in all of them, picture identical
in all but the first (the rebuilt renderer's first frame).

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
index f49da12..8b97381 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
@@ -160,7 +160,7 @@ void PipelineCache::LoadCache(const std::atomic_bool& stop_loading,
 
 void PipelineCache::SwitchCache(u64 title_id, const std::atomic_bool& stop_loading,
                                 const VideoCore::DiskResourceLoadCallback& callback) {
-    if (GetProgramID() == title_id) {
+    if (GetProgramID() == title_id && curr_disk_cache) {
